## Summary

| Severity | Count | Top Issue |
|----------|-------|-----------|
| 🔴 Critical | 0 | — |
| 🟡 Moderate | 7 | Triple-regex chain in `Underscore()` (4 allocs/call × millions of calls) |
| ℹ️ Info | 1 | Unsealed `InflectionRule` |

**Top priority:** Findings #1 and #2 dominate — `Underscore()` and `Pascalize()` are on your stated hot path and collectively allocate 6-16 intermediate strings per call. A single-pass `StringBuilder`/`string.Create` rewrite of `Underscore()` and a span-based fix in `Pascalize()` would eliminate the majority of GC pressure.

